WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.095 --> 00:00:03.470
(ethereal music)

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:05.650
- [Narrator] High above
a small town in France

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:07.193
sits a beautiful chapel.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:10.950
It's a long way to the top.

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:12.410
But you know what they say:

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:15.393
the bigger the climb, the closer to God.

00:00:16.411 --> 00:00:19.860
(contemporary music)

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.080
Chapel Saint-Michel d'Aiguilhe,

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.910
otherwise known as Saint
Micheal of the Needle,

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:27.380
is located in Le Puy-En-Velay,

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:31.070
a town roughly six hours away from Paris.

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:34.210
Built atop an extinct
volcanic plug that is believed

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:36.630
to have formed over two million years ago,

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:39.930
this church rises nearly
300 feet from the ground

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:42.453
and is dedicated to the Archangel Michael.

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:49.800
The church was commissioned
by a bishop in the year 951

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:52.570
who wanted to commemorate
his 1,000 mile journey back

00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:54.323
from the Pyrenees Mountain Range.

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:58.420
On average, the site
receives just over 65,000

00:00:58.420 --> 00:00:59.960
visitors each year.

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:04.240
And at 268 steps, the
climb to the top is long.

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:06.790
But the view is quite a reward

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:10.103
with a 360-degree look
at the town including

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:12.653
the surrounding volcanic formations.

00:01:20.352 --> 00:01:23.435
(electronic pinging)

